it's fine. Hmm, let me do exact match \u2014 if it fails, the test is wrong and I'd need to fix. Risk assessment: pyyaml has had this message since forever. OK exact.\n\nFor the ParserError test, use \"{invalid\" hmm wait \u2014 actually let me reconsider. \"{invalid\" \u2192 tokens: FLOW-MAPPING-START, SCALAR(\"invalid\"), then stream end. Parser: parse_flow_mapping_key \u2192 after scalar, expects ',' or '}' \u2192 gets stream end \u2192 ParserError(\"while parsing a flow mapping\", start_mark, \"expected ',' or '}', but got ''\"? hmm.\n\nActually the parser error for this: \n\n```\nyaml.parser.ParserError: while parsing a flow mapping\n  in \"<unicode string>\", line 1, column 1\nexpected ',' or '}', but got '<stream end>'\n  in \"<unicode string>\", line 1, column 9\n```\n\nHmm, the problem is \"expected ',' or '}', but got '<stream end>'\"? Hmm, actually I think the problem text is \"expected ',' or '}', but got ''\" \u2014 no. Let me think: ParserError raised via:\n\n```python\n        raise ParserError(\"while parsing a flow mapping\", self.marks[-1],\n                \"expected ',' or '}', but got %r\" % token.id, token.start_mark)\n```\n\ntoken.id for stream end is '<stream end>'. So problem = \"expected ',' or '}', but got '<stream end>'\". Hmm wait, but actually for flow mapping end detection, the parser uses peek and if token is FlowMappingEnd \u2192 done; elif token is FlowEntry (',') \u2192 continue; else error. Hmm, but actually there's a subtlety: `parse_flow_mapping_key`:\n\n```python\n    def parse_flow_mapping_key(self, first=False):\n        ...\n        if not self.check_token(FlowMappingEnd):\n            if self.check_token(FlowEntry):\n                ...\n            else:\n                token = self.peek()\n                yield self.process_empty_key(token)\n                ...\n```\n\nI don't remember exactly. The point: it raises ParserError. problem_mark.index = 8 (end of stream, after \"invalid\" which ends at index 7... \"{invalid\"